WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.112
Who is this for?

2
00:00:01.112 --> 00:00:02.151
Three groups.

3
00:00:02.151 --> 00:00:03.537
Developers build it.

4
00:00:03.537 --> 00:00:06.054
The identity engineers own the accounts,

5
00:00:06.054 --> 00:00:09.088
the exclusion group and
the record of every drill.

6
00:00:09.088 --> 00:00:11.663
And security operations receive the alert,

7
00:00:11.663 --> 00:00:14.238
and hear about each
drill before it happens.

8
00:00:14.238 --> 00:00:16.847
The reader app gets six Graph permissions,

9
00:00:16.847 --> 00:00:20.275
each the least privileged for
its call, and nothing more.

10
00:00:20.275 --> 00:00:22.507
Two of those choices are worth noticing:

11
00:00:22.507 --> 00:00:26.701
reading whether an account is enabled
or synchronized needs the full user

12
00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:30.700
read permission, because those
properties aren't in the basic profile.
